From 121cc101d4338c10116dd9ff2e78e9b5fa648b5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:25:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 159/206] F79: revert F37's shape-A native call emission -- it
 cannot run

F37 (954cd28dcf9, plus 9f740d6104b) made every link_lazily native call in
precompiled mode emit

  ldr x16,[PP,#slot]; nop; nop; asr x16,x16,#1; ldr x30,[THR,x16]; blr x30

with the pool slot holding SmiTag(bootstrap_native_wrapper_entry_point_offset).
That bought "ours=92, matches theirs" on measure_dd_emission.sh. The count was
never runtime-validated: dd_runtime_check.sh is the only check in verify_all.sh
that executes a compiled AOT program, and it had not been run since before F37
landed. The first run after rebuilding ProductARM64 at HEAD dies on the very
first snapshot it is asked to run:

  si_signo=SIGSEGV, si_code=SEGV_ACCERR, si_addr=0x7000000000000095
  dart::TransitionSafepointState::TransitionSafepointState(dart::Thread*)
  <- ThreadStackResource <- StackResource

Bisected: 232849c87d8 (F37's parent) is good, dd_runtime_check.sh reports
0 failure(s); 954cd28dcf9 is the first bad commit, identical signature. The
9 commits between it and HEAD touch only analyze_snapshot_api_impl.cc.

Root cause: Thread caches no entry point for the CallBootstrapNative *stub*.
CACHED_ADDRESSES_LIST (thread.h:262) caches only the address of the C function
NativeEntry::BootstrapNativeCallWrapper, so `blr x30` lands directly on a C
function with Dart registers in x0/x1 instead of the (Dart_NativeArguments,
Dart_NativeFunction) C ABI -- hence the garbage Thread* 0x95 -- and skips the
exit frame, vm_tag and NativeArguments setup GenerateCallNativeWithWrapperStub
performs. Independently, NativeCallPattern (instructions_arm64.cc:82) recovers
both pool indices by decoding this exact call site, so LinkNativeCall and
CodePatcher::{Get,Patch}NativeCallAt cannot decode shape A either.

No local correction of the pool slot fixes this; there is no offset in the
current Thread layout that makes the sequence correct. Choosing one would mean
inventing a dispatch protocol and calling it Shorebird's, which is what rule 3
forbids -- and per F35 this instruction pattern has already been misread once.
So this reverts the emission and records both constraints at the site.

Cost, stated plainly: measure_dd_emission.sh native_patched goes ours 92 -> 0,
theirs 92. That gap is real again and F37 should be reopened.

Post-revert: dd_runtime_check.sh 0 failure(s); all three inputs that crashed
(gen_kernel --help, fresh hello snapshot, hello.dill -> .so) now run, and the
snapshot prints the pinned EXPECTED block. --self-test output is byte-identical
to the known-good parent (4 failures + the F78 threshold bug, unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/compiler/backend/il_arm64.cc b/runtime/vm/compiler/backend/il_arm64.cc
index e84972c9aa1..26dce5d8544 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/compiler/backend/il_arm64.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/compiler/backend/il_arm64.cc
@@ -1328,32 +1328,33 @@ void NativeCallInstr::EmitNativeCode(FlowGraphCompiler* compiler) {
                      link_lazily() ? ObjectPool::Patchability::kPatchable
                                    : ObjectPool::Patchability::kNotPatchable);
   if (link_lazily()) {
-    if (FLAG_precompiled_mode) {
-      // Shorebird shape A: dispatch via thread field instead of Code* stub.
-      // Emits: ldr x16,[PP,#slot]; nop; nop; asr x16,x16,#1; ldr x30,[THR,x16]; blr x30
-      // Pool slot stores SmiTag(bootstrap_native_wrapper_entry_point_offset)
-      // so the untagged value is directly usable as a THR base-register offset.
-      const intptr_t thr_off =
-          compiler::target::Thread::bootstrap_native_wrapper_entry_point_offset();
-      // Store SmiTag(thr_off) as kTaggedObject so the pool entry type matches
-      // Shorebird's encoding (Smi stored as tagged object, not raw immediate).
-      // At runtime: ldr x16 loads thr_off*2; asr x16,x16,#1 untags to thr_off.
-      const Smi& thr_off_smi = Smi::ZoneHandle(Smi::New(thr_off));
-      const intptr_t idx = __ object_pool_builder().AddObject(thr_off_smi);
-      __ LoadWordFromPoolIndex(R16, idx);    // ldr x16,[PP,#s] + nop;nop in precompiled mode
-      __ AsrImmediate(R16, R16, 1);          // asr x16,x16,#1  (untag Smi)
-      CLOBBERS_LR({
-        __ ldr(LR, compiler::Address(THR, R16));  // ldr x30,[x26,x16]
-        __ blr(LR);                               // blr x30
-      });
-      compiler->EmitCallsiteMetadata(
-          source(), DeoptId::kNone, UntaggedPcDescriptors::kOther, locs(),
-          nullptr);
-    } else {
-      compiler->GeneratePatchableCall(
-          source(), *stub, UntaggedPcDescriptors::kOther, locs(),
-          compiler::ObjectPoolBuilderEntry::kResetToBootstrapNative);
-    }
+    // F79: F37 replaced this, in precompiled mode, with Shorebird's "shape A"
+    // ldr x16,[PP,#slot]; nop; nop; asr x16,x16,#1; ldr x30,[THR,x16]; blr x30
+    // where the pool slot held SmiTag(bootstrap_native_wrapper_entry_point_
+    // offset). That emission was reverted here because it cannot run, and the
+    // "ours=92 matches theirs" parity it bought was a pure instruction-shape
+    // count that is invariant to whether the code works. Two facts constrain
+    // any future attempt; neither was known when F37 landed:
+    //
+    //  1. Thread caches no entry point for the CallBootstrapNative *stub* --
+    //     CACHED_ADDRESSES_LIST (thread.h) only caches the address of the C
+    //     function NativeEntry::BootstrapNativeCallWrapper. So blr'ing through
+    //     any existing THR slot lands on a C function with Dart registers in
+    //     x0/x1 instead of (Dart_NativeArguments, Dart_NativeFunction), and it
+    //     faults in TransitionSafepointState's ctor reading a garbage Thread*.
+    //     It also skips the exit frame, vm_tag and NativeArguments setup that
+    //     GenerateCallNativeWithWrapperStub does.
+    //  2. NativeCallPattern (instructions_arm64.cc:82) recovers both pool
+    //     indices by decoding this call site, so LinkNativeCall and
+    //     CodePatcher::{Get,Patch}NativeCallAt break on shape A even if the
+    //     branch target were right.
+    //
+    // Before re-landing shape A, establish what their pool slot actually
+    // indexes -- per F35 this instruction pattern has already been misread
+    // once -- rather than choosing an offset that makes a count match.
+    compiler->GeneratePatchableCall(
+        source(), *stub, UntaggedPcDescriptors::kOther, locs(),
+        compiler::ObjectPoolBuilderEntry::kResetToBootstrapNative);
   } else {
     // We can never lazy-deopt here because natives are never optimized.
     ASSERT(!compiler->is_optimizing());
-- 
